<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Camel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">656 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-fitna">First Fitna</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">Camel</a> was fought in 656 CE near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basra">Basra</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> Ali and forces led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aisha">Aisha</a>, Talha and al-Zubayr, who demanded vengeance for the murdered caliph Uthman. It takes its name from the camel on which Aisha rode during the fighting. Ali won, but it was the first battle between Muslims in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-fitna">First Fitna</a>, the civil war that undermined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-camel.jpg" alt="Battle of the Camel" width="285" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ali_and_Aisha_at_the_Battle_of_the_Camel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
